  "acceptedDifferences": {
    "columnOrdinals": "The parent has dropped-column slots. Compare active column identities, types, defaults, collations, storage, nullability, generation metadata, and column ACLs. Physical attribute numbers are not portable.",
    "mediaOrigin": "Three named routines and one product_media constraint use the exact persistent development media project. Check all six occurrences before accepting the target-specific comparison.",
    "access": "Use individually granted application access. Nine parent public tables give client roles REFERENCES, TRIGGER and MAINTAIN. Fifteen give the service role those privileges and TRUNCATE. Development needs none. Schema and sequence effective privilege digests match the parent at base. Development also removes seven direct EXECUTE grants on three trigger-only functions. Explicit grants are required on new app objects.",
    "preservedAuthHook": "The prefix database retains the original loyalty trigger OID, name, and handler OID. Its renamed handler must have the canonical rewards body and receive exactly one enabled AFTER INSERT FOR EACH ROW invocation. Verify prior OIDs separately before accepting this normalized identity.",
    "providerIntegration": "The parent has six catalog notification hooks. Development enables none while Search and webhook isolation remain unqualified. Supabase supplies Storage service triggers and Realtime. Their inventory is checked independently from the application schema; the observed parent publication has no table members.",
    "scope": "Includes only pinned development SQL additions. Separately installed production support, marketing delivery and marketing events packages remain outside this Catalog release."
  }
